Direct primitives: dynamics.py, state_spec.py, rotations.py, objective.py,
schedule.py; sampling.py adapts envs/mdp/commands.py return-to-go updates.
Local changes: imports/formatting; StateSpec becomes an nn.Module with registered
scale buffers for device/dtype movement and checkpoints; objective.py accepts a
minimal rollout record supplied by the PHP adapter.

The surrounding networks.py and train.py adapt the revised SiLU/fixed-scale
policy/critic, learned termination head, normalized autoregressive loss,
horizon-normalized BPTT, GAE and env-step UTD scheduling to PHP. PHP retains its
own teacher observations/termination conditions, sphere hands, terrain, bounded
executed actions, replay boundary masks, and balanced selected-skill resets (five
step/climb skills by default). Rewards now match the original local SuperMimic
tracking definition, including clean-action rate penalties; the contact reward
and learned contact head have been removed from new training. legacy_networks.py
is only for loading pre-migration v2 policies, under the parent LICENSE.
Upstream experiment results do not establish performance of this adaptation.
Motion datasets retain their respective licenses.
